## Part 7 — Quick Reference Card

Assemble a short "cheat sheet" the developer pastes at the top of every AI session.

### 7.1 How to run things
```
Install:      make install (or: uv sync --frozen --extra dev)
Run tests:    make test (or: pytest tests/ -v)
Lint:         uv run python -m ruff check <paths>
Typecheck:    uv run python -m mypy <paths>
Format:       uv run python -m ruff format <paths>
```
Detect these from the Makefile and CI workflow. Cite the source.

### 7.2 Key files the AI should always read before editing
List the 5–8 most important context files. Example:
```
AGENTS.md        → Development conventions and repo map
CI.md            → Mandatory checks before push
TESTING.md       → How to write tests (ReplDriver, fixtures)
config/config.py → How configuration works
pytest.ini       → Test marks and structure
ruff.toml        → Linting rules
```

### 7.3 The "one paragraph" repo summary
Write a single paragraph (3–5 sentences) describing what this repo does, how it is structured, and what the AI should keep in mind when editing it. This is what the developer pastes first in every AI session.

