## Part 8 — Final CONTEXT.md Assembly

Assemble all of the above into a single `CONTEXT.md` file structured as follows:

```markdown
# CODEBASE CONTEXT — [Repo Name]
Generated by CodeMind on [date]. Re-run after major refactors.

## What This Repo Does
[Part 7.3 one-paragraph summary]

## Tech Stack
[Part 1 output]

## Naming Conventions
[Part 2 DO/NOT THIS pairs]

## Architecture Rules
[Part 3 layer map + import directions]

## Technical Patterns
[Part 4 — HTTP client, error handling, config, testing, async, types]

## Integration Pattern
[Part 5 — how to add new integrations]

## NEVER DO (Hard Rules for AI)
[Part 6 numbered list]

## Quick Reference
[Part 7.1 commands + 7.2 key files]
```

**Self-check before emitting:**
- [ ] Every convention cites a real file — no invented rules
- [ ] NEVER DO list sourced from actual repo prohibitions, not general best practices
- [ ] Commands verified against Makefile and CI workflow
- [ ] Absence notation used where something is not detected
- [ ] Output is a single clean Markdown file, ready to paste into any AI agent session

